  <section id="status-codes" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Status codes across the contract</h2>
    <p>Counting each declared response once per operation gives this picture of what a client must be ready to decode:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Declared on</th><th>Typical body</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>200</td><td>242 operations</td><td>Resource, array, nullable value or <code>Envelope</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>201</td><td>28 operations</td><td>The created record (for example <code>POST /api/projects</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>204</td><td>1 operation</td><td>No body</td></tr>
        <tr><td>400</td><td>206 operations</td><td><code>BadRequest</code>, <code>EnvBadRequest</code> and family-specific variants</td></tr>
        <tr><td>401</td><td>269 operations</td><td><code>Unauthorized</code> (bearer middleware)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>403</td><td>101 operations</td><td><code>Forbidden</code> / <code>EnvForbidden</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>404</td><td>149 operations</td><td><code>NotFound</code> / <code>EnvNotFound</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>405</td><td>30 operations</td><td><code>EnvMethodNotAllowed</code> / <code>KeyedMethodNotAllowed</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>409</td><td>29 operations</td><td><code>Conflict</code> / <code>EnvConflict</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>500</td><td>264 operations</td><td><code>InternalError</code>, <code>EnvInternal</code>, <code>KeyedInternal</code> and family variants</td></tr>
        <tr><td>501, 503</td><td>1 operation each</td><td>Endpoint-specific</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Every error is an Effect tagged error, so its JSON body always contains a <code>_tag</code> discriminator next to its fields. There are three body families, inherited from the legacy handlers so existing clients keep working:</p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="Plain error (message only)">
{"{ \"_tag\": \"NotFound\", \"message\": \"Project not found\" }"}
    </DocCode>
    <DocCode language="json" title="Envelope error">
{"{ \"_tag\": \"EnvNotFound\", \"success\": false, \"message\": \"Material not found\", \"errors\": null }"}
    </DocCode>
    <DocCode language="json" title="Keyed error (a few library routes)">
{"{ \"_tag\": \"KeyedInternal\", \"error\": \"Failed to load components\" }"}
    </DocCode>
    <p>Success envelopes mirror the error envelope: <code>&#123; success: true, message, data &#125;</code>, where <code>data</code> may be <code>null</code>. The <code>EnvelopeOpt</code> variant omits <code>message</code> when the handler did not provide one. Switch on <code>_tag</code> rather than on the presence of <code>message</code> or <code>error</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="request-lifecycle" class="doc-section">
    <h2>How a request is processed</h2>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 780 150" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Request lifecycle" style="max-width:780px;font:12px system-ui">
<defs><marker id="apar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="currentColor"/></marker></defs>
<g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2">
<rect x="5" y="40" width="110" height="56" rx="8"/><rect x="135" y="40" width="120" height="56" rx="8"/><rect x="275" y="40" width="120" height="56" rx="8"/><rect x="415" y="40" width="120" height="56" rx="8"/><rect x="555" y="40" width="100" height="56" rx="8"/><rect x="675" y="40" width="100" height="56" rx="8"/>
<path d="M115 68H133M255 68H273M395 68H413M535 68H553M655 68H673" marker-end="url(#apar)"/></g>
<g fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle">
<text x="60" y="64">client</text><text x="60" y="80" opacity=".7">fetch / SDK</text>
<text x="195" y="64">route match</text><text x="195" y="80" opacity=".7">method + path</text>
<text x="335" y="64">bearer check</text><text x="335" y="80" opacity=".7">401 Unauthorized</text>
<text x="475" y="64">schema decode</text><text x="475" y="80" opacity=".7">400 on bad input</text>
<text x="605" y="64">handler</text><text x="605" y="80" opacity=".7">access + logic</text>
<text x="725" y="64">encode</text><text x="725" y="80" opacity=".7">success / _tag</text>
<text x="390" y="125" opacity=".7">x-session-token picks the acting account; absent or invalid falls back to the local profile</text></g></svg>
    <ol>
      <li>The router matches method and path. Unknown routes never reach a handler.</li>
      <li>The bearer middleware compares the token in constant time. A missing or wrong token stops the request with 401 before any decoding.</li>
      <li>Path, query, headers and body are decoded against the operation's schemas. Structural problems become 400 without running business code.</li>
      <li>The handler resolves the acting account, checks ownership or organization membership (403/404) and runs the service.</li>
      <li>The result is encoded with the declared success schema, or the failure with its tagged error schema and status.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="non-json" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Responses that are not JSON</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Media type</th><th>How to consume</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>POST /api/ai/chat/stream</code></td><td><code>text/event-stream</code></td><td>Read incrementally; each <code>data:</code> line is one typed assistant event.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>GET /api/projects/&#123;id&#125;/events</code></td><td><code>text/event-stream</code></td><td>Live project events; reconnect and re-read state after a drop.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>GET /api/plugins/bootstrap.js</code></td><td><code>application/javascript</code></td><td>Loaded by the plugin host, not parsed as JSON.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>GET /api/plugins/serve</code></td><td><code>application/octet-stream</code></td><td>Plugin file bytes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>GET /api/download</code></td><td><code>application/zip</code></td><td>Save as a file; use <code>response.blob()</code> or stream to disk.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The generated Promise SDK rejects a streaming response whose content type is not <code>text/event-stream</code> with <code>ClientError("UnsupportedContentType")</code>, and a single SSE event larger than 16 MiB with <code>SseEventTooLarge</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="raw-fetch" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Calling the API without a client</h2>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Minimal typed fetch wrapper">
{"type TaggedError = { _tag: string; message?: string; error?: string }\n\nasync function call<T>(base: string, token: string, method: string, path: string, body?: unknown): Promise<T> {\n  const response = await fetch(new URL(path, base), {\n    method,\n    headers: {\n      authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\n      ...(body === undefined ? {} : { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" }),\n    },\n    body: body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(body),\n  })\n  if (response.status === 204) return undefined as T\n  const payload = await response.json()\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const failure = payload as TaggedError\n    throw new Error(`${response.status} ${failure._tag}: ${failure.message ?? failure.error}`)\n  }\n  return payload as T\n}\n\nconst project = await call<{ id: string; name: string }>(\n  process.env.CADCAMFUN_URL!, process.env.CADCAMFUN_TOKEN!,\n  \"POST\", \"/api/projects\", { name: \"Bracket\" },\n)"}
    </DocCode>
    <p>Prefer the generated clients in TypeScript: they know each operation's success status and declared error statuses, and treat anything else as <code>UnexpectedStatus</code> instead of guessing.</p>
  </section>

